{"Race condition between CountDevices check and device creation/update in CreateOrUpdateDevice allows concurrent requests to exceed the device limit": 0.8108435869216919, "updateDevice returning ErrDeviceLimitReached when rowsAffected == 0 is semantically incorrect - zero rows affected could mean the device doesn't exist within the time window, not that the limit was reached": 0.9495000839233398, "Potential time skew in limit check - CountDevices uses time.Now().UTC() while subsequent upsert operations use device.UpdatedAt, which may differ significantly": 0.17602331936359406, "GrafanaBootConfig class property anonymousDeviceLimit lacks explicit type annotation, causing TypeScript to infer narrower type 'undefined' instead of 'number | undefined' required by GrafanaConfig interface": 0.9189786314964294, "Duplicate constant anonymousDeviceExpiration defined in both database.go and api/api.go risks drift if one is updated without the other": 0.6528682112693787, "Test for device limit doesn't verify that existing devices can still be updated when limit is reached": 0.315170556306839, "Missing CreatedAt field in test device struct may cause issues with DB constraints or default value handling": 0.599806547164917}